pkg:Evidence_v1_2_0 a quality:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Gate transcript for code-abundance-rdodi v1.2.0 (MINOR release)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "MINOR release responding to user finding that the report was 'mechanic, insufficient and shamefully low in academic and industrial quality.' Root cause: v1.1.0's Stage 3 document was a flat, one-paragraph-per-concept glossary -- descriptive restatement of the article with no theoretical mechanism, no critical evaluation, and no synthesis, which is structurally insufficient for the report genre regardless of prose quality per paragraph. Fix, in two parts. (1) Stage 2 domain TBox/ABox bumped to v1.1.0 (MINOR, backwards-compatible addition): added CriticalAnalysisAndConclusion (1 top-level class + 3 leaves: DeveloperDemandCritique, MetricValidityAndSelectionBiasCritique, SynthesisAndImplications), giving the report genuine argument-evaluation and synthesis structure it previously lacked entirely. Re-verified: Stage2.A (parse), Stage2.B (HermiT consistency, re-run for real), Stage2.C (SHACL, 0 violations), Stage2.D (7 top-level, 18 leaf, depth OK), Stage2.E (18/18 exemplars), Stage2.F (10/10 BP-D24 predicates on both files), Stage2.G (filenames) -- all PASS. (2) Stage 3 document substantially rewritten end to end, all 25 sections (not just the 4 new ones): every section now explains its cited theory or evidence at the level of mechanism (Goldratt's five focusing steps; Jevons' price-elasticity/rebound mechanism, not just name-checked) and states explicitly what kind of evidence each industry case is (independent vs. GitLab's own commercial product) rather than treating all four uniformly. Section length rose from an average of roughly 60-80 words to 193 words (min 82, max 381). All mechanical gates re-verified PASS: Stage3.A (198 triples), Stage3.B (SHACL, 0 violations), Stage3.E.cov/E.sub (26 structural individuals, all substantive), Stage3.src (26 real-sourced). Manual gates re-verified: Stage3.C (25=25 section-class count match), Stage3.D (exact label match), Stage3.H (25/25 sourced to Stage 2 class). Stage3.F (reference rule) caught one real defect on first run -- the new Synthesis and Implications section referred to 'the article's claims' without naming Staples by year anywhere in its own text -- fixed and re-verified 0 uncited across all 26 individuals. DOCX companion regenerated from the same v1.2.0 TTL (no re-authoring), grew from 5 to 8 pages, verified by LibreOffice conversion and visual page inspection. DISCLOSED, NOT FIXED HERE: Stage 4 (the interactive page ABox and HTML) still reflects the prior 21-section structure from v1.1.0 and has not been updated to the new 25-section document. Cross.B and Stage4.E would not currently pass if re-run against code_abundance_document_v1_2_0.ttl. This is stated plainly rather than silently left inconsistent; bringing Stage 4 into alignment with the new document structure is separate, deferred work."@en ;
    pub:transcriptSHA256 "05815315d3d30043386354b7f1f00d9756ccbab2712953bc557c5b96a01357b1"^^xsd:string .
